// lawha-server's own config, because the repo root's extends `react-app` and
// this is a Node server with no JSX in it.
//
// COMMENTS, NOT A "//" KEY. The first draft of this file carried its prose in a
// top-level `"//"` array, which is a common trick and is rejected outright here:
// ESLint 7 validates the config schema and answers `Unexpected top-level
// property "//"` — not for this directory, for the whole run, so `yarn test:code`
// fails across all 791 files. ESLint strips `//` and `/* */` from .eslintrc.json
// before parsing it, so real comments are both legal and safer.
//
// `root: true` stops ESLint searching upwards. That is deliberate and stays —
// but until now this file also had `rules: {}`, so `root: true` meant every file
// under lawha-server resolved EXACTLY ZERO rules while appearing to be linted.
// `yarn test:code` walked 13,000 lines of server and found nothing it was
// capable of finding. Measured: 0 rules here against 305 for an app file. That
// is the worst shape a gate can take — it reports 0 errors over 59 files, and
// the 0 is guaranteed rather than earned.
//
// What is switched on is what earns its keep on a Node service:
//
//   eslint:recommended        real defects — unreachable code, duplicate keys
//   prettier/prettier         one format, mechanically enforced
//
// prettier/prettier is not cosmetic here. `yarn test:other` only covers
// css,scss,json,md,html,yml; TypeScript formatting in this repo is enforced
// through this rule and nowhere else, so until now no .ts file under
// lawha-server had ever been checked by anything.
//
// What is deliberately NOT on: plugin:@typescript-eslint/recommended. Measured
// before deciding — it adds 184 no-non-null-assertion warnings, and `!` is used
// on purpose here after a check the checker cannot see. A rule that fires 184
// times on existing, correct code is a rule people learn to ignore.
//
// `no-undef` is OFF, which is standard for TypeScript and not laziness: it does
// not know ambient types, so it reported `NodeJS` and `RequestInit` as undefined
// across 14 sites. The compiler already answers this question and
// `yarn test:typecheck:server` already asks it.
//
// STILL NOT LINTED, and said out loud rather than left to be discovered:
// `scripts/*.mjs` — 8,800 lines including the three suites `yarn test:server`
// runs. `test:code` passes `--ext .js,.ts,.tsx`, which excludes .mjs, so those
// files are invisible to the linter no matter what this file says.
{
  "root": true,
  "env": { "node": true, "es2021": true },
  "parser": "@typescript-eslint/parser",
  "parserOptions": { "ecmaVersion": 2022, "sourceType": "module" },
  "plugins": ["@typescript-eslint", "prettier"],
  "extends": ["eslint:recommended", "prettier"],
  "rules": {
    "prettier/prettier": "error",
    "no-undef": "off",
    "no-unused-vars": "off",
    "@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars": ["error", { "argsIgnorePattern": "^_", "varsIgnorePattern": "^_" }]
  }
}
